@startuml
title Comment + Interaction — System overview
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho

actor "Web / Mobile user" as User
component "API Gateway\nJWT + correlation + routing" as Gateway
component "Feed / BFF" as BFF
component "Post Service\nPost + Bookmark owner" as Post
component "Profile Service" as Profile
component "Eureka" as Eureka

package "Owned synchronous scope" #E8F5E9 {
  component "Comment Service\ncontent, replies, deletion, counts" as Comment
  database "Comment PostgreSQL\nFlyway namespace: comment" as CommentDB
  component "Interaction Service\nLIKE ledger + counters + actor state" as Interaction
  database "Interaction PostgreSQL\nFlyway namespace: interaction" as InteractionDB
}

queue "Kafka" as Kafka #FFF3E0
component "Notification Service\nUUID + idempotency pending" as Notification #FFF3E0

User --> Gateway : JWT, API request
Gateway --> Comment : /comment/api/v1/...
Gateway --> Interaction : /interaction/api/v1/...
Gateway --> Post : /post/api/v1/...

Comment --> Post : Feign: validate POST\n(current public API; internal CR pending)
Interaction --> Post : Feign: validate POST
Interaction --> Comment : Feign + internal token\nvalidate COMMENT
Comment --> CommentDB : local transaction
Interaction --> InteractionDB : ledger + counter\nsame local transaction

Comment ..> Eureka : discover post-service
Interaction ..> Eureka : discover post/comment-service

BFF --> Comment : batch comment counts
BFF --> Interaction : batch reaction counters
BFF --> Profile : batch author display data

Comment ..> Kafka : future: versioned events + outbox
Interaction ..> Kafka : future: versioned events + outbox
Post ..> Kafka : future: PostDeletedV1 + outbox
Kafka ..> Notification : future: idempotent UUID consumer
Kafka ..> Interaction : future: CommentDeletedV1/PostDeletedV1
Kafka ..> Comment : future: PostDeletedV1

legend right
  Solid arrows = implemented synchronous flow
  Dotted arrows = proposed cross-team/event flow
  Each owned service has its own database
  Bookmark stays in Post; Notification owns notifications
endlegend
@enduml
